The [38;5;10mscanf[0m return value is never checked. This is the subtlest part: on a partial parse, conversions stop at the first failure and the remaining variables keep their prior values. So empty input leaves [38;5;10mx=0[0m → [38;5;10mError: x != 1[0m, while [38;5;10m1[0m alone leaves [38;5;10my=123[0m → [38;5;10mError: x == 1 but y != 2[0m. Both verified against the C.[0m[0m
