Integer overflow was the one place I refused to guess. I probed the C binary with a value chosen to discriminate two plausible models: [38;5;10m18446744073709551617[0m (2⁶⁴+1) has low 32 bits of exactly 1, so mod-2³² wrapping would print [38;5;10mOk![0m. It printed the error instead — glibc saturates to [38;5;10mLONG_MAX[0m per [38;5;10mstrtol[0m, [3mthen[23m truncates to [38;5;10mint[0m ([38;5;10m-1[0m). Meanwhile [38;5;10m4294967297[0m and [38;5;10m8589934593[0m do yield [38;5;10mx == 1[0m, confirming plain truncation for in-range [38;5;10mlong[0ms. My accumulator reproduces exactly that: saturate at [38;5;10mi64::MIN[0m/[38;5;10mMAX[0m, then [38;5;10mas i32[0m.[0m[0m
